node_modules

# Output
.output
.vercel
.netlify
.wrangler
/.svelte-kit
/build

# `nix build` drops this symlink into the repo root. Ignored here rather than
# left to a contributor's global ignore file, because oxlint reads *this* file
# to decide what to walk — and a lint run that descends into the built server
# bundle reports thousands of errors in generated code.
/result
/result-*

# Android has no entry here on purpose. The Gradle project is committed — it is
# source, and every manifest, theme and icon edit lives in it — and it carries
# its own `android/.gitignore`, generated by `cap add android` and committed with
# the rest. That file already excludes the build outputs, `local.properties`, and
# the three generated artefacts that matter most: `app/src/main/assets/public` is
# the entire web bundle, recopied by `cap sync` on every build, and
# `capacitor.config.json` / `capacitor.plugins.json` are derived from
# capacitor.config.ts and the installed plugin set. Restating any of it here
# would be two files to keep in agreement for no gain.

# Signing keystores. Nothing here should ever hold one — the release key lives
# outside the tree and reaches CI as a base64 secret (.github/workflows/release.yml)
# — but `keytool` writes to the working directory by default, so the one command
# that creates a keystore is precisely the one that drops it in the repo root.
# This is the net under that. android/.gitignore ships the same two lines
# commented out; uncommenting them there would only cover the subtree.
*.jks
*.keystore

# Database (the SQLite file, plus WAL and shared-memory sidecars)
/.data

# Illustration sources — megabytes of PNG per exercise, and the model can make
# them again from scripts/illustrations/PROMPTS.md. The traced SVGs are the
# artefact worth keeping.
/scripts/illustrations/raw

